<title>YEMEN: Yemen oil output at 377,000 bpd - oil official.</title>
<headline>Yemen oil output at 377,000 bpd - oil official.</headline>
<dateline>SANAA 1997-08-18</dateline>
<text>
<p>Yemen's current oil output stands at about 377,000 barrels per day (bpd), an oil ministry official said on Monday.</p>
<p>&quot;Some 200,000 bpd came from Masila, 150,000 bpd from Marib, 25,000 from Jannah and 2,000 barrels from Shabwa,&quot; the official told Reuters.</p>
<p>Independent U.S. company Hunt Oil operates the Marib (Block 18) and Jannah (Block 5) fields, while Canadian Occidental Petroleum Ltd operates Masila's Block 14, and Nimir Petroleum runs Shawba's Block 4.</p>
<p>Non-OPEC Yemen, a small Arab oil producer, targets production of 400,000 bpd by the end of the year.</p>
</text>
